  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 131 AM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nMid-level ridging will continue to be the main driver of our \nforecast for the upcoming period. While a Four-Corners ridge remains \ngenerally stationary, the Bermuda high will gradually stretch \neastward across Florida. A weak wave looks to ride below the \nsouthern edge of the Bermuda high toward the weekend and makes its \nway toward the Texas coast. Moisture appears limited - so no \nsubstantial rain chances expected. Will maintain some 10-20% rain \nchances with the seabreeze daily through the end of the week. For \nthe weekend could see slightly higher (20-25%) PoPs around the \nVictoria Crossroads. \n\nTemperatures remain near seasonal normals through the period with \nhighs between 100 and 105 west and in the mid and upper 90s east. \nHeat index values will top out primarily between 105 and 110. Low \ntemperatures will be mainly in the 70s. RH values do fall to near \nlow levels west, however fuel moisture are normal and should limit \nelevated fire weather concerns.",
